  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Kenya Capacity Development Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the Capacity Building programme is that Caritas Kenya and the Dioceses increase efficiency and effectiveness in promoting sustainable and integral human development at all levels through facilitating in technical development programming and representation. It is thus envisaged that the Capacity Programme will steer Caritas Kenya in making progress towards achievement of its strategic goals as per the Commission Strategic Plan 2007-09.   The programme has had to put the necessary measures in place to support the achievement of Commission objectives. These include identifying the key personnel to coordinate key Commission focus areas,   ensuring that the staff have the necessary skills, identifying key capacity needs in the Dioceses and addressing them, strengthening the interface role of the Commission relative to the Dioceses and stakeholders at all levels and enhancing the commission role as a development agency among other development players in Social Development arena. 

The specific objectives of the programme include, to strengthen Caritas Kenya governance systems and procedures for effective coordination, facilitation and representation of the Diocesan Development programmes; implement a staff development programme in Caritas Kenya; enhance Capacity of KEC on Social Development; and to strengthen the advocacy role of Caritas Kenya</narrative>
  </description>
